IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bda-debt-agreements`

-- Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Cth) Part IX, ss 185, 185C, 185E, 185EC, 185F, 185G, 185H, 185K, 185LB, 185LC, 185M, 185N, 185NA -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_bankruptcy-act-1966.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Scenario facts used (workbench scenarios/au/wa/cradle-to-grave-jake/facts.json and SCENARIO.md): Jake Harding, born
-- 2006-08-30; debts of $41,000 and collectors (k064, 2037-02-06); a debt agreement proposed by him, gated by the Official
-- Receiver and accepted by a majority of creditors in value (k065, 2037-04-20); "Five years at $690 a month" from 2037-06-01
-- (k066); completion on 2042-05-31 (k075). From 2033-11-01 to 2038-06-01 he lives in a rented unit in Gosnells under the
-- Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA); he owns no home until a contract of 2042-02-18. The scenario's supplied facts give
-- the threshold as "indexed; about $150,000 in unsecured debts": that figure is the scenario's, not the Act's, and is used
-- as an INPUT. NOT in the scenario, and ASSUMED here: that the agreement is made on 2037-06-01 when the plan starts; that he
-- has no divisible property; a likely after tax income of $52,000; that he gave the proposal 3 days after signing it; and the
-- split of the $41,000 among creditors used in the vote, which is illustrative only.

